OpenBMC evb-ast2600: order the MCTP serial link before mctpd so auto-discovery installs the route

Rev-2 (PLDM Type 2) BMC-side delta on top of patch 0004. With the Zephyr node
now answering baseline MCTP control commands with the tag-owner bit cleared on
its responses (Zephyr control-responder fix) and the kernel AF_MCTP dump
busy-loop fixed on this image (patch 0010), mctpd's SetupEndpoint enumerates
the endpoint itself: it runs Get Endpoint ID, adopts EID 18, adds the kernel
route and neighbour, queries Get Message Type Support, and publishes the
endpoint on D-Bus so pldmd's platform-mc discovers and polls it. No manual
"mctp route add" is needed.

The remaining blocker was a startup-ordering race. The stock unit ordered
itself After=mctpd.service, so mctpd started before the serial link existed.
mctpd snapshots the kernel link map exactly once at startup into its
route-query netlink handle (ctx->nl_query) and never refreshes it from the
monitor socket; a link that appears after mctpd is therefore invisible to
peer_route_update(), which fails with "BUG: Unknown ifindex" and the route to
the discovered endpoint can never be installed (pldmtool -m 18 then returns
rc=-7). Fix: bring the link up before mctpd and run SetupEndpoint after it.

Split mctp-local.service into two units:

  * mctp-local.service - creates the serial link, brings mctpserial0 up and
    assigns the local EID (8). Ordered Before=mctp-local.target; mctpd.service
    is already After=mctp-local.target, so the interface exists (up, with a
    local EID) before mctpd enumerates. The "mctp link serial" process is the
    line-discipline holder, so it stays the long-running ExecStart.
  * mctp-setup-endpoint.service - a oneshot that runs the SetupEndpoint busctl
    call after mctpd is up (needs its D-Bus BusOwner interface) and after the
    link exists. The endpoint is a separate Zephyr QEMU instance that may boot
    after the BMC, so the call is wrapped in a bounded retry loop (40 x 3 s).

Verified on a cold boot with the fixed kernel image and Zephyr firmware (two
QEMU instances, zero manual steps): mctp-local/mctpd/mctp-setup-endpoint all
active, SetupEndpoint succeeds once, mctpd auto-installs the kernel route
"eid min 18 max 18 dev mctpserial0" and neighbour, endpoints/18 is published
on D-Bus, and pldmtool base GetTID/GetPLDMTypes + platform GetPDR/
GetSensorReading over -m 18 all answer rc=0.

---

diff --git a/meta-evb/meta-evb-aspeed/meta-evb-ast2600/recipes-phosphor/mctp/files/mctp-local.service b/meta-evb/meta-evb-aspeed/meta-evb-ast2600/recipes-phosphor/mctp/files/mctp-local.service
index 533df4c..90ef973 100644
--- a/meta-evb/meta-evb-aspeed/meta-evb-ast2600/recipes-phosphor/mctp/files/mctp-local.service
+++ b/meta-evb/meta-evb-aspeed/meta-evb-ast2600/recipes-phosphor/mctp/files/mctp-local.service
@@ -1,18 +1,23 @@
 [Unit]
 Description=MCTP configuration for serial ttyS0 (AST2600 UART1)
-After=mctpd.service
-Before=pldmd.service
-BindsTo=mctpd.service
+# Bring the MCTP-over-serial link up BEFORE mctpd starts. mctpd snapshots the
+# kernel link map once at startup into its route-query netlink handle and does
+# not refresh it from the monitor socket, so a link that appears after mctpd is
+# invisible to peer_route_update() ("BUG: Unknown ifindex") and the route to a
+# discovered endpoint can never be installed. mctpd.service orders itself
+# After=mctp-local.target, so ordering this unit Before that target guarantees
+# the interface exists (and is up, with a local EID) when mctpd enumerates.
+Before=mctp-local.target
 
 [Service]
+# mctp link serial is the line-discipline holder: mctpserial0 exists only while
+# this process lives, so keep it as the long-running ExecStart (Type=simple).
 Type=simple
 ExecStartPre=stty -F /dev/ttyS0 115200 litout -crtscts -ixon -echo raw
 ExecStart=mctp link serial /dev/ttyS0
 ExecStartPost=sleep 3
 ExecStartPost=mctp link set mctpserial0 up
 ExecStartPost=mctp addr add 8 dev mctpserial0
-ExecStartPost=mctp route add 18 via mctpserial0
-ExecStartPost=busctl call au.com.codeconstruct.MCTP1 /au/com/codeconstruct/mctp1/interfaces/mctpserial0 au.com.codeconstruct.MCTP.BusOwner1 SetupEndpoint ay 0
 
 [Install]
-WantedBy=mctpd.service
+WantedBy=mctp-local.target
diff --git a/meta-evb/meta-evb-aspeed/meta-evb-ast2600/recipes-phosphor/mctp/files/mctp-setup-endpoint.service b/meta-evb/meta-evb-aspeed/meta-evb-ast2600/recipes-phosphor/mctp/files/mctp-setup-endpoint.service
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..c3771aa
--- /dev/null
+++ b/meta-evb/meta-evb-aspeed/meta-evb-ast2600/recipes-phosphor/mctp/files/mctp-setup-endpoint.service
@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@
+[Unit]
+Description=MCTP endpoint auto-discovery (SetupEndpoint on mctpserial0)
+# Runs after mctpd is up (needs its D-Bus BusOwner interface) and after the
+# serial link exists (mctp-local.service, ordered before mctp-local.target).
+# SetupEndpoint enumerates the remote endpoint (Get Endpoint ID over physical
+# addressing): mctpd assigns/accepts its EID, adds the kernel route and
+# neighbour itself, queries Get Message Type Support, and publishes it on D-Bus
+# so pldmd's platform-mc discovers it. No manual "mctp route add" is needed.
+After=mctpd.service mctp-local.service
+Requires=mctpd.service mctp-local.service
+Before=pldmd.service
+BindsTo=mctpd.service
+
+[Service]
+Type=oneshot
+RemainAfterExit=yes
+# The endpoint (a Zephyr QEMU instance) may boot after the BMC, so retry the
+# BusOwner call until the node answers.
+ExecStart=/bin/sh -c 'n=0; while [ $n -lt 40 ]; do busctl call au.com.codeconstruct.MCTP1 /au/com/codeconstruct/mctp1/interfaces/mctpserial0 au.com.codeconstruct.MCTP.BusOwner1 SetupEndpoint ay 0 && exit 0; n=$((n+1)); sleep 3; done; exit 1'
+
+[Install]
+WantedBy=mctp.target
diff --git a/meta-evb/meta-evb-aspeed/meta-evb-ast2600/recipes-phosphor/mctp/mctp_%.bbappend b/meta-evb/meta-evb-aspeed/meta-evb-ast2600/recipes-phosphor/mctp/mctp_%.bbappend
index 14948b1..7462ea8 100644
--- a/meta-evb/meta-evb-aspeed/meta-evb-ast2600/recipes-phosphor/mctp/mctp_%.bbappend
+++ b/meta-evb/meta-evb-aspeed/meta-evb-ast2600/recipes-phosphor/mctp/mctp_%.bbappend
@@ -4,15 +4,26 @@ FILESEXTRAPATHS:prepend := "${THISDIR}/files:"
 # can speak PLDM to an external endpoint reachable over a UART. The second
 # QEMU -serial backend is wired to AST2600 UART1, which Linux exposes as
 # /dev/ttyS0 (serial0 alias). Modeled on meta-evb-fvp-base.
+#
+# Split into two units so ordering is correct for mctpd's auto-discovery:
+#   mctp-local.service        - creates the serial link + local EID, ordered
+#                               Before=mctp-local.target (i.e. before mctpd),
+#                               because mctpd snapshots the link map once at
+#                               startup and never refreshes it.
+#   mctp-setup-endpoint.service - runs SetupEndpoint after mctpd is up so mctpd
+#                               enumerates the peer, installs the kernel route
+#                               and neighbour, and publishes it on D-Bus.
 SRC_URI:append = " \
   file://mctp-local.service \
+  file://mctp-setup-endpoint.service \
   file://mctpd.conf \
 "
 
-SYSTEMD_SERVICE:${PN} += "mctp-local.service"
+SYSTEMD_SERVICE:${PN} += "mctp-local.service mctp-setup-endpoint.service"
 
 do_install:append() {
     install -m 0644 ${UNPACKDIR}/mctp-local.service ${D}${systemd_system_unitdir}/
+    install -m 0644 ${UNPACKDIR}/mctp-setup-endpoint.service ${D}${systemd_system_unitdir}/
     install -d ${D}/etc/
     install -m 0644 ${UNPACKDIR}/mctpd.conf ${D}/etc/mctpd.conf
 }

